title: Reichslandbund (RLB) faces existential threat...
subtitle: Rural wrath engulfes the Germany...
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: rural_rlb_collapse >= 1 and not rlb_banned

= National Rural League's doom

{!
<div id="rlb-figure" class="face-figure2" style="position:relative; transition: all 1.5s ease-in-out;">
  <img id="rlb-img-normal" src="img/rlb.png" alt="RLB" class="face-img"
       style="transition: opacity 1.5s ease-in-out;" />
  <img id="rlb-img-banned" src="img/rlb_1.png" alt="RLB banned" class="face-img"
       style="position:absolute; top:0; left:0; opacity:0; transition: opacity 1.5s ease-in-out;" />
</div>
!}

With the rural populace protesting, blocking provisions, terrorizing the countryside, attacking Junkers, sabotaging machinery, breaking tools, and committing acts of terror despite starving, the old conservative parties were unable to respond, as their interests lay strictly with the Junkers, big landowners, and other upper classes.

With local rural leagues defecting one after another, [? if rlb_party_leader = "Martin Schiele": [+ rlb_party_leader +] pushed for integration with the DNVP in the face of imminent collapse. However, other rural representatives opposed the idea, forcing Martin Schiele to defect to the DNVP alone. With its president's defection, the RLB no longer held legitimacy among other leagues and rural organizations. ?] [? if rlb_party_leader = "Karl Hepp": Karl Hepp declared a coalition between his defected rural leagues (in March 1928) and the remaining leagues, reforming the RLB into a new entity. ?] Gustav von Kalckreuth, now the sole president of the organization, declared its disbandment and [? if cnbl_votes > 0: joined the CNBLP. ?] [? if cnbl_votes <= 0 and nsdap_votes >= 4: joined the NSDAP. ?] [? if cnbl_votes <= 0 and nsdap_votes < 4: formed his own splinter league. ?]

- @continue

@continue
title: Old imperial remnant collapses.
on-arrival: {!
Q.rlb_banned = 1;
this.achieve('landlicher_zorn')
!}

